  (extremely detailed version):\nLinear Models:\nMode 1:\n{m1_eq}\nMode         
  2:\n{m2_eq}\n\nSwitching Guards:\n- Mode 1 -> Mode 2: Occurs when x1 ≈        
  {avg_m1_m2[0]:.3f} (observed x2 ≈ {avg_m1_m2[1]:.3f})\n- Mode 2 -> Mode 1:    
  Occurs when x1 ≈ {avg_m2_m1[0]:.3f} (observed x2 ≈ {avg_m2_m1[1]:.3f})\nThe   
  switching logic is primarily driven by the x1 coordinate reaching these       
  symmetric thresholds.\n\n### 3. Additional context (if relevant):\nThe        
  system exhibits periodic switching behavior, and the coefficients suggest a   
